--- ### Implementation Challenges 
1. Pagination for book listing - Add query parameters (e.g., ?page=1&limit=10). - Modify the service to slice data based on page and limit. - Include pagination metadata in responses (e.g., total pages, current page). 
2. Search functionality for books API - Add query parameters (e.g., ?search=title:Harry). - Implement filtering logic in the service layer to match fields like title or author. 
3. User authentication and authorization - Use JWT middleware to verify tokens. - Add role-based access control (e.g., admin vs. user) in the service layer. - Store user data in a database.

 --- ### Real-world Scenarios 
1. Supporting multiple data sources - Abstract data access with a repository pattern. - Use dependency injection to switch between sources (e.g., file, MongoDB).    
2. Real-time updates - Implement WebSockets (e.g., Socket.IO) or Server-Sent Events. - Notify clients of resource changes (e.g., new book added). 
3. Rate limiting and API quotas - Use express-rate-limit middleware to limit requests per user/IP. - Track usage in a database or Redis for quota enforcement.
